        "original_id": "1911aa22-c4ec-5230-87a2-7e898b489dd1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Bowie, Tony Visconti\n- Products: Blackstar, \"Dollar Days\"\n- Places: New York City, The Magic Shop, Human Worldwide Studios\n- Topics: David Bowie's death, album recording, album release\n\nFacts:\n- David Bowie released his twenty-fifth and final studio album, Blackstar, on 8 January 2016.\n- \"Dollar Days\" is the sixth track on David Bowie's twenty-fifth and final studio album, Blackstar.\n- Blackstar was largely recorded in secret in New York City at The Magic Shop and Human Worldwide Studios with David Bowie's longtime co-producer Tony Visconti and a group of local jazz musicians.\n- David Bowie died on 10 January 2016 at his New York City apartment after suffering from liver cancer for the previous 18 months.\n- David Bowie's death occurred two days after the release of Blackstar, which coincided with his 69th birthday.",
